.TH "RAPTOR-WHATIF" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-whatif \- compare one or more changes with the open model
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor whatif\fR [\-h] [\-\-change PATH=VALUE] [\-\-name N] [\-\-note TEXT] [\-\-change\-file FILE] [\-n N] [\-\-precision P] [\-\-requirement EXPR] [\-\-seed N|new] [\-j N] [\-\-timeout DURATION] [\-\-progress {auto,bar,json,none}] [\-\-save FILE] [\-f {text,json}] MODEL
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the model and each scenario with the same seed and compare them by paired trials: the same change costs far less noise than two independent batches. A scenario is the model plus a short list of PATH=VALUE changes; the model file is never modified.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-change\fR \fIPATH=VALUE\fR
one change for the scenario, repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fIN\fR
name of the scenario the \-\-change options make (default Scenario)
.TP
\fB\-\-note\fR \fITEXT\fR
why the scenario is tried, shown with its row
.TP
\fB\-\-change\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR
JSON list of {name, changes, note} scenarios
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-trials\fR \fIN\fR
runs per scenario (default: the model's own)
.TP
\fB\-\-precision\fR \fIP\fR
size the batch first with run\-to\-precision, e.g. 10%%
.TP
\fB\-\-requirement\fR \fIEXPR\fR
e.g. system.ao>=0.995 (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-seed\fR \fIN|new\fR
salt every random stream (default: the fixed seed 'raptor run' uses, so the numbers match a plain run)
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fIN\fR
cores to run on (default 1). Any 2 or more give the same numbers; they differ, equally validly, from 1
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIDURATION\fR
stop the study after DURATION, e.g. 90s, 10m (default 30m); what it measured by then is reported and marked partial
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI{auto|bar|json|none}\fR
progress on stderr (auto: only on a terminal; json: one object per line; none, or \-q, for silence)
.TP
\fB\-\-save\fR \fIFILE\fR
write the scenario definition(s) as JSON
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR
output format (default text)
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Compare one change with the model on 500 paired runs.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor whatif pump.rbds \-\-name 'Faster repair' \-\-change 'block:Pump A.repair_params=2.5' \-n 500\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Several scenarios from a file, each checked against a target.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor whatif pump.rbds \-\-change\-file options.json \-\-requirement 'system.ao>=0.995' \-f json\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
